  Proof checked: with e_i = d_i - s/N (sum 0), rotate just after a maximiser m of the
  partial sums T_k. Then every new partial sum is T_. - T_m <= 0, so S'_k <= (s/N)k <= alpha k
  because s <= alpha N. Each rotation class has <= N members and contributes >= 1 confined word.
