==============================================================================
C3. The suffix pair-counting form and the capacity bound
==============================================================================
  Claim: for a < B, with M_v = 2^{b+1}, H = 2^{B-a}, y_v = 3^{-j} r_v mod M_v,
         Q_hi(v) = floor(y_v / H)  and  q = M_v/H = 2^{s+1-B}.
  Also sum_x h(x)^2 = #{(v,v') : floor(y_v/H) = floor(y_v'/H)} <= (H/2) * |V|,
  since the y_v are distinct odd residues and each interval holds <= H/2 odd values.
  classes checked: 86   Q_hi/q-form violations: 0   y_v even: 0   capacity-bound violations: 0

  Required: delta_U + delta_V < 2(1-sigma*) = 0.100088946
  and delta_U + delta_V = 2(1 - tau_eff), so this is the SAME condition as tau_eff > sigma*.
  Interpretation correction: a finite tau_eff below sigma* is compatible with a uniform
  exponent tau at constant cost C >= q^(tau - tau_eff); e.g. q=256, tau=0.96, tau_eff=0.830
  gives C >= 2.056.
